# Auto-commit

After a coherent change in this repo, create a **local** git commit. Do not push unless asked.

## Identity (repo-local only)

This repository already sets `user.name` and `user.email` in `.git/config`. Do **not** change global git config, and do **not** write a personal address into this file.

If those values are missing, set them with `git config user.name` / `user.email` inside this repo only.

## Message

Follow the user-level Google / Conventional Commits rule (`~/.cursor/rules/git-commit.mdc`):

```
<type>(<scope>): <imperative summary>
```

English subject, optional body for why. Examples: `feat(launcher): remember last skin and apply on open`, `fix(overlay): paint wallpaper onto .sand-shell`.

Never `--amend` a commit that is not yours, has been pushed, or that the user did not ask to rewrite. Never `--no-verify`. Never commit `.env`, credentials, or `Grok Bot.app`.
